# Default-deny build context. Only the inputs needed by `pip install .` and the
# one shipped warm script are allowed; tests, workflows, docs, deployment
# units, local state, credentials and Git history never enter the build
# context. A new build input must be added here explicitly.
*
!pyproject.toml
!README.md
!LICENSE
!ci_burst
!ci_burst/**

# The warm script the image ships (see the Dockerfile). Each parent directory
# is allowed and then emptied again, so the one file enters the context on every
# builder, including those that skip an excluded parent without looking inside.
!deploy
deploy/*
!deploy/runner
deploy/runner/*
!deploy/runner/image
deploy/runner/image/*
!deploy/runner/image/warm-cache.sh

# Re-exclude generated bytecode inside an allowed directory (later pattern wins).
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
